ef 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134777 #edb/ref 1061 27407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134777 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6bc95e77-3f78-52e2-890a-fdf8d97395f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134777 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135091 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that if $X$ is a binomial random variable in which there are $n$ experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}.\n$$\n\nIt can be shown that the expected value, variance, and standard deviation of a binomial random variable $X$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135091 #edb/ref 1065 4452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135091 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "872af947-d3c7-525f-8bb9-21d55de36921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186135091 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186447210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186447211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186447212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186447213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186447214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1045 "Mean and Variance of the Binomial Distribution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186447210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447174 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "67edc56b-a9ee-5fab-b142-813c8f1ec3bc" #edb/ref 17